# Audi A6 C6 four-door saloon, 2004-2011.
#
# The third A6: the larger C6 body with the single-frame grille, the sharper
# shoulder line and the longer wheelbase. The Avant and allroad are different
# bodies and are not represented.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Audi_A6
#
# Dimensions 4.916 x 1.855 x 1.459 m, wheelbase 2.843 m.
#
# Shape reference: image 1 is a near-side view, not verified as a true level
# profile; the front and rear three-quarters show the lamps and tail. The
# flank is estimated; the limitation is recorded.
#
# Colours: grade (d); no UK chart was established. Black, silver, grey and
# blue are plain names. Weights 20, 18, 17, 15, total 70, provisional.
#
# Speed 230 km/h. Comfort 92/318, on the line 180 + 1.5 x 92. Classes 3,4.
# Dates are road presence: 2004 intro, retires staggered 2028-2031.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/audi-a6-c6.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/audi-a6-c6.dae. References:
# citycars/references/audi-a6-c6/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: there is no door-shoulder scallop or wheel-arch flare,
# the lamps are flat panels rather than sculpted units, and the rear window is
# more upright than the photograph's. At 128 px the large single-frame grille,
# slim lamps and long shoulder line read as a C6 A6.


obj=citycar
name=AudiA6C6(Black)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=20
intro_year=2004
intro_month=1
retire_year=2031
retire_month=6
speed=230
class=3,4
maximum_comfortable_journey_minutes=92
maximum_tolerable_journey_minutes=318

